rds, so searching for `_` matches every customer. There's also no `LIMIT`, so the result size is unbounded.

Suggested replacement:

```ts
export async function findInvoicesByCustomer(name: string) {
  const pattern = `%${name.replace(/[\\%_]/g, "\\$&")}%`;
  return db.query(
    `SELECT i.* FROM invoices i
     JOIN customers c ON c.id = i.customer_id
     WHERE c.name LIKE $1
     LIMIT 500`,
    [pattern],
  );
}
```

The `LIMIT 500` cap is a placeholder; pick whatever number fits your UI or add pagination. It's also worth adding a test that searches for `'` and `%` so this can't come back.

nside the loop runs a separate database query for each line that has a promo, and each query waits for the previous one. A cart with 50 promo lines means 50 queries in a row. Look up the unique codes together instead:

```ts
const codes = [...new Set(lines.flatMap(l => l.promo ? [l.promo] : []))];
const promos = new Map(codes.map((c, i) => [c, loaded[i]]));
// where loaded = await Promise.all(codes.map(loadPromo))
```

A single `WHERE code = ANY($1)` query would be better still.

**Nit:** `for (let i = 0; i <= lines.length - 1; i++)` adds nothing. `for (const l of lines)` handles `await` fine.

